 See `examples/owner-corrections.example.json`.
 
+## Page-region retry
+
+When the first enhance retry still holds an item for OCR quality, a second scripted pass renders the full PDF page at 400 dpi (`retry.page_region.dpi`) and crops the question image region using the pdftohtml boxes in `extracted/raw.xml`. The crop is enhanced at scale 1 (already high dpi), then both fidelity OCR passes run again. The same strict gate still decides export. This pass is logged in `export/ocr-retry.json` with `stage` set to `page_region`.
+
+## AI vision hook
+
+If both scripted retries still hold the item, a committed `review/ai-reads.json` (or `review/ai-reads/QUESTION.json`) may supply a transcription. The hook in `scripts/ai_vision.py` is off by default (`ai_vision.enabled` is false, `provider` is `none`) because Actions has no AI key. A later local provider can be plugged in through `hook_module`; the hook never auto-fills empty files.
+
+An AI transcription is accepted only when:
+
+- every OCR word with confidence 90 or above, from both original fidelity passes (not a later failed retry), appears in the AI text in order
+- every PDF text-layer word is still covered (by the AI text plus the already extracted stem and choices)
+- type and key rules pass, and the site v2 schema still accepts the question
+
+Accepted items are exported with `answer.reviewer_needed` set to true. The `ai_vision` provenance (source, confidence, image sha256, transcribed text) is written to `export/ai-vision.json` in raw-exam reports, not to site-file fields the schema forbids. If the AI text is not accepted, the item stays on the review sheet and the AI text is stored as `ai_suggestion` only. `owner_text` and `owner_decision` stay empty.
+
+See `examples/ai-reads.example.json`.
+
